    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Ice cores were collected from Barrow Environmental Observatory in Barrow, Alaska, in 2013 as part of the Next Generation Ecosystem Experiment (NGEE). Each core was drilled from a different location at varying depths. A few days after drilling, the cores were stored in coolers packed with dry ice and flown to Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory (LBNL) in Berkeley, CA. 3-dimensional images of the cores were constructed using a medical X-ray computed tomography (CT) scanner at 120kV. Images were reconstructed to resolutions of 2.56 pixels per millimeter."
    ],
